{
	"nodes":[
		{
			"id":"fabf68db62e84f75",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Adjusted Assets\n\"UAL\", \n\"PAL\", \n\"BTC-USD\", \n\"SPY\", \n\"VIX\", ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1300,
			"y":-860,
			"width":220,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"9dac6bf9daa5fb23",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Financial Instruments\nAll Financial instruments have Open, High, Low, Close, Volume, and Adjusted \n## Assets\n\"UAL\", \n\"PAL\", \n\"BTC-USD\", \n\"SPY\", \n\"VIX\", \n\n## Fred Tickers\n\"DGS10\", \n\"FEDFUNDS\", \n\"CPIAUCSL\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1720,
			"y":-860,
			"width":380,
			"height":440
		},
		{
			"id":"9532b7a68f8116c4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Log Adjusted Returns\nIt used to normalize returns and are calculated as the natural logarithm of the ratio of the current price to the previous price..\n$$\nr=ln(\\frac{P_t}{P_{t-1}})\n$$",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1040,
			"y":-860,
			"width":420,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"700310701dd0ab1c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Simple Returns\nIt measure the gain or loss generated on an investment relative to the amount of money invested.\n$$\nr_i=\\frac{P_t}{P_{t-1}}-1\n$$",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1040,
			"y":-620,
			"width":420,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"6f57963a7ea111c2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Fred Tickers?\n\"DGS10\", \n\"FEDFUNDS\", \n\"CPIAUCSL\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1300,
			"y":-420,
			"width":220,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"ce85e029e0907feb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Neoclassical Paradigm\nClassic financial concepts that treats the financial system as a linear, rational, mechanical engine that naturally tends toward a stable equilibrium.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":120,
			"y":-1440,
			"width":380,
			"height":240
		},
		{
			"id":"e04d1a8c4ab3b23b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Complex Adaptive System Paradigm\nIt views markets not as sterile machines, but as biological ecosystems where feedback loops, friction, and shifting participant behavior constantly warp the environment out of equilibrium.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":540,
			"y":-1440,
			"width":380,
			"height":240
		},
		{
			"id":"2fe36d0302594d6a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Random Walk\nAsset price movements are modeled as Geometric Brownian motion where log-returns are independent and identically distributed normal random variables - a random walk. ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":120,
			"y":-1180,
			"width":380,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"d4e5f5d74ae160ac",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Normal Distribution",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":120,
			"y":-960,
			"width":380,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"9b8dd347a4bd5fbc",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"#  Fat Tails",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":540,
			"y":-1180,
			"width":380,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"3926312ff5debbea",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"#  Anomalous Diffusion",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":540,
			"y":-960,
			"width":380,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"1f38639f59717150",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Asset Price Movements\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-240,
			"y":-1080,
			"width":260,
			"height":190
		}
	],
